## Appendix B: the loading bug

In October we found a loading bug. A timing test on the on-board computer loaded our checkpoint with `strict=False`. The image had transformers {{audit_tf}}, and under that version {{audit_dropped}} encoder tensors did not match. They were dropped without an error. The test timed a random encoder, and we voided its latents. We then traced how every other use loaded the model. {{audit_trained}} ran the trained model and {{audit_random}} ran a random one, the timing test. The world-model block of VLA-JEPA, which one diagnostic above uses, loads all {{wm_keys}} of its keys.

## Appendix C: the probe

Every outcome probe in Table @tab:controls is this function (`repro/gaps/scripts/analyze_controls.py`):

```python
def loso(X, y, groups):
    p = np.zeros(len(y))
    for g in np.unique(groups):
        te = groups == g
        sc = StandardScaler().fit(X[~te])
        m = LogisticRegression(C=1.0, class_weight="balanced", max_iter=5000).fit(sc.transform(X[~te]), y[~te])
        p[te] = m.predict_proba(sc.transform(X[te]))[:, 1]
    return p
```

Every number in this paper is generated by `paper/make_paper.py` from `repro/*/expected/`; its source is in `paper/numbers.json`.
